        lines.append('- ' + name + ' (product_id ' + ref + '): past due ' + money(due) + ', ' + str(days) + ' days late, ' + ('late' if late else 'early') + ' band. Floor (lowest amount allowed): ' + money(floor) + '. Any amount from ' + money(floor) + ' to ' + money(due) + ' is accepted. Deadline (latest date): ' + spoken(deadline) + ' (' + deadline.isoformat() + '). Persuasion attempts: ' + str(attempts) + '. If the full amount is too much, say exactly: I can offer ' + money(floor) + ' by ' + spoken(a1) + ' instead. The rest stays overdue. If a date after the deadline is asked, say exactly: The latest date I can record is ' + spoken(deadline) + '. Can you pay on ' + spoken(deadline) + '? (a no to this is a flat refusal). If a vague period is given, ask once: Which exact day? If still none, propose ' + spoken(deadline) + '. If the amount is below the floor, say exactly: I cannot record an amount below ' + money(floor) + '. Can you pay ' + money(floor) + '?')
    table = []
